# FOREWORD

1.	This QSP is developed under the authority of the Commander Military Personnel Generation Training Group (MPGTG) and is in accordance with the following references:

a.	A-P9-050 Series, Canadian Forces Manual of Individual Training and Education (CFITES); and

b.	A-PD-055-002/PP-002, job based specification (JBS) for CYBER OP MOSID 00378 dated 31 January 2017.

2.	This QSP was developed in collaboration with representatives from the Directorate of Cyber Operations Force Development (D Cyber Ops FD), the Canadian Forces Network Operations Centre (CFNOC), the Canadian Forces School of Communications and Electronics (CFSCE), the Royal Military College (RMC) Computer Security Lab, and Director Information Management Engineering and Integration (DIMEI).

3.	This QSP consists of specific Performance Objectives (POs) in Chapter 2 and Enabling Objectives (EOs) in Chapter 4. A candidate will achieve the qualification when the standards listed in the POs have been met.

4.	This QSP is effective upon approval.

5. 	Suggestions for amendments to this QSP shall be forwarded through the chain of command to COS MPGTG and CFSCE Standards. Final approvals for amendments is COS MPGTG.

6.	The designated TE for this training is indicated below:

