1 Job complexity: Average-the complexity of the job is the same as what is expected from tasks in the NCMG/OGS.  Complex-the complexity of the job is greater than what is expected from tasks in the NCMGS/OGS.

2 The TP board will define any real impact on training.  Chapter 2 of the QSP remains job-oriented.  Therefore, this annex will not try to cover all possible training limitations and/or impact. However, any significant potential impact should be noted there by the QSPWB.  

3 The Asterisk indicates change made to the Task Statement or creation of a new Task. The plus sign (+) indicates that the task has not been trained previously.  

**TRAIN/NO-TRAIN SELECTION CRITERIA:**

Criterion A: Previously trained/qualified on other courses. Skills and knowledge already possessed by trainee.

Criterion B: Trained at a lower level but member has gained enough experience to perform competently this level.

Criterion C: Gained through experience without formal training.

Criterion D:  Specialized task; not performed by all or majority of jobs at a particular rank level (requires specialized training).

Criterion E: Difficulty. Task not difficult, formal training not required.

Criterion F: Importance. Task not important, little impact on mission.

Criterion G: Frequency. Task rarely performed. Formal training not required.

Criterion H: Time performing. When task is performed, relatively little time spent on it.

Criterion I: Probability of deficient performance. Personnel will not have a problem learning this task on the job.

Criterion J: Time between job entry and performance. Task will not be performed for a long time after training (high risk of skill fade).

Criterion K: Lack of equipment. Currently there is no equipment in the CAF inventory to adequately train this task.

Criterion L: Theatre mission specific training.

