| Comments (other point of interests / concerns) | As per Annex F, there is potential for many of the activities and exercises associate with this training to ultimately be delivered online/remotely (i.e., distance learning via a cyber range). Costs will be significantly reduced if this can be achieved. Training delivery occurring in the area where the candidates are employed (e.g., the NCR), vice sending the candidates to the TE, is predicated on the idea that CFSCE is not well suited to delivering this type of training. The main issue is Internet access; CFSCE accesses the Internet via GPnet, which is filtered. Filtered access means that candidates will not be able to access resources (e.g., the Exploit DB) using DND/CAF connectivity, thereby negatively impacting learning. By selecting a third party location to train in (e.g., room in a local hotel or conference centre), unfiltered Internet access can be assured. Furthermore, the amount of infrastructure required to support the training lends itself to conducting training outside of DND facilities, as it is essentially laptops for the candidates, a 1U or 2U server, a network printer, and a switch/router connected to the Internet. As such, additional costs will be incurred if a commercial space is required to conduct the training. |

